    "title": "Deliver a chart with traceable data and alternative access",
    "intro": "A chart handed to stakeholders needs more than a working image file. The deliverable should identify its source, calculation, scope and limitations, and offer another way to understand the evidence when the visual alone is insufficient.",
    "sections": [
      [
        "Choose the visual reasoning",
        "Keep the source snapshot, transformation code, chart settings and dependency versions traceable. A title cannot replace metric definitions, inclusion rules or data lineage. Preserve a table of the plotted values so a reviewer can check that marks and labels agree with the underlying calculation.",
        "Provide a concise textual summary of the main comparison and its limits, plus an accessible table when appropriate. Alternative text should communicate the purpose and relevant evidence rather than simply naming chart colors. A static PNG by itself does not provide a full semantic data structure for assistive technologies."
